# Serve the English page at /en without a redirect, so people whose browser
# locale points elsewhere have a stable URL to share and come back to.
# The 200 keeps the path as /en, and that is what stops assets/translations.js
# from bouncing the visitor to their browser language. Only the smooth root
# auto-switches language, so /angry/ and /student/ need no alias.
#
# The destination has to be / rather than /index.html: the asset router
# normalises /index.html back to / and answers with a 307, which would land
# the visitor on the very path that auto-switches.
/en / 200
